        {
          "id": "india-ltcg-fpi-review-2026-11-05",
          "headline": "Sitharaman open to reviewing capital gains tax on foreign investors",
          "summary": "Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman said on Monday she would consider calls to review the long-term capital gains tax on shares, after industry body PHD Chamber and, per Reuters, market regulator SEBI urged that it be scrapped for foreign portfolio investors. Foreign funds have pulled out more than $30 billion from Indian stocks so far in 2026, and Nomura puts their share of Indian equities at a record-low 14%. No decision has been announced.",
          "why_it_matters": "A tax cut for foreign investors could help reverse record outflows that have weighed on the Nifty and the rupee this year.",
          "importance": 4,
          "lead": false,
          "verified": false,
          "note": "Single source: CNBC (citing Reuters). Only a review is under consideration; no decision taken.",
          "published_at": "2026-11-04T19:04:00-05:00",
