          "id": "currency-rupee-midday-2026-11-05",
          "headline": "Rupee hovers near 94.4-94.55 as stock rally offsets dollar demand",
          "summary": "The rupee opened at 94.36 per dollar and slipped to 94.55 in early trade, PTI reported, before trading near 94.43 around 1:40 pm. Strong foreign buying of shares (about Rs 7,000 crore on Wednesday) and Brent near $94-95, far below last week's levels, are supporting it, while dealers cite importers' dollar buying. Reports differ on Wednesday's closing level, so the day's change is not stated here.",
          "why_it_matters": "Cheaper oil and foreign inflows are the rupee's two biggest supports; if Hormuz tensions lift oil again, that cushion shrinks.",
          "importance": 4,
          "lead": false,
          "verified": false,
          "note": "Single source: PTI (via HDFC Sky/DT Next); midday level from Yahoo Finance. Sources disagree on Wednesday's close (94.46 to 94.65).",
